  "result": "Perfect! All 137 tests pass. Let me verify the complete implementation:\n\n**Summary of VAT implementation:**\n\n1. **src/invoices.js** \u2014 Added VAT calculation:\n   - New `lineVAT(line)` function: calculates VAT on the amount after discount\n   - Updated `invoiceTotals` to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n   - Formula: `total = subtotal - discount + vat`\n   - VAT is rounded per line and summed for the invoice\n\n2. **src/render.js** \u2014 Updated to show VAT:\n   - Shows \"VAT: \u20acamount\" line when VAT > 0\n   - Appears just above the Total line\n   - All amounts formatted via `formatEuros()`\n\n3. **Tests** \u2014 Added 13 comprehensive VAT tests covering:\n   - Line VAT calculations with/without discounts\n   - VAT with 0%, 9%, and 21% rates\n   - Mixed VAT rates on multiple lines\n   - VAT with customer tier discounts\n   - Complete invoices with all features combined\n   - Fixed 9 existing tests to account for VAT in totals\n\n**Key behavior:**\n- VAT is computed PER LINE on (lineTotal - lineDiscount), rounded per line\n- Invoice VAT is the SUM of rounded line VATs, never a percentage of invoice total\n- Totals are clamped at 0 (never negative)\n- No amount goes below zero, as required",
